WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.300
The US

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.102
military is striking back

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:03.803
after a deadly drone attack

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.739
killed an American contractor

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:08.041
and wounded five service members.

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:08.908
The Pentagon says that

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:10.510
an Iranian made drone

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.645
struck a base in northeast Syria.

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:14.180
An official telling CNN

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.615
that it was a one way drone

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:17.317
that intentionally crashed

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:18.752
into its target.

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:19.419
President Biden

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:20.820
responded with airstrikes

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:21.488
against groups

00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:23.823
affiliated with Iran's Revolutionary

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:25.158
Guard in Syria.

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:26.226
What you're looking at

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:27.927
is social media video that appears

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:30.397
to show the flaming aftermath of the U.S.

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:30.897
strikes.

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:32.198
I think we're going to go to the Pentagon

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:32.499
right now

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:33.199
where we're expecting

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:34.834
to get a briefing on this.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:37.170
Let's see if we can listen in on that.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.171
In northeast

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:39.139
northeast Syria,

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:41.741
at approximately 1:38 p.m.

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.176
local time.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:44.944
Secretary Austin, at the direction

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:46.980
of President Biden, authorized U.S.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:47.614
Central Command

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:48.648
forces to conduct

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:51.217
precision strikes into eastern Syria

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:52.952
against facilities

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:53.753
used by groups

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:55.055
affiliated with Iran's

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:57.824
Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps.

00:00:57.824 --> 00:00:59.659
The airstrikes were conducted in response

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:01.494
to yesterday's attack,

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:01.961
as well

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:03.396
as a series of recent attacks

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:05.432
against coalition forces in Syria

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:08.735
by groups affiliated with the IRGC

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:12.172
In terms of air strike details, two U.S.

00:01:12.172 --> 00:01:14.641
Air Force F-15 fighter aircraft

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:16.042
assigned to U.S.

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:17.477
Air Forces Central

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:18.778
and based in the CENTCOM

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:22.348
area of responsibility struck two IRGC

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:23.550
affiliated facilities

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.518
at approximately 7:40 p.m.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:28.488
Eastern time or 2:40 a.m.

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:29.522
local

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:32.325
the facilities were located near Dozier

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:35.061
in eastern Syria,

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:36.663
and we're continuing to assess

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:38.398
the outcome of the strikes.

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:39.732
Initial indications are that

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:41.634
the facilities were destroyed

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:42.135
in regards

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:42.902
to any militant

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:45.438
casualties were still assessing.

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:46.506
These precision strikes

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:48.341
were intended to protect and defend U.S.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:49.676
personnel And the U.S.

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:51.778
took proportionate and deliberate action

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:52.612
intended to limit

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:54.547
the risk of escalation

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:56.749
and minimize casualties.

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:57.550
As Secretary

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:58.918
Austin said in his statement,

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:00.553
no group will strike our troops

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:02.055
with impunity.

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:03.356
Again, Secretary Austin,

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:04.724
along with the Department of Defense,

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:05.492
offer our thoughts

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:06.025
and prayers

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:06.593
to the family

00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:08.595
and colleagues of the American contractor

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:09.762
who was killed

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:10.263
and with those

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:12.065
who are wounded in the attack.

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:13.600
Our forces deployed in Syria

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:14.100
continue

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.368
to conduct their important mission

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:17.237
in support of the international coalition

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:19.472
to ensure the enduring defeat of ISIS.

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:22.142
Separately, Secretary Austin

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:23.643
and Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:24.210
General Milley,

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.345
testified yesterday

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:26.846
before the House Appropriations

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:29.682
Subcommittee on Defense to discuss

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:33.353
the president's fiscal year 2024 budget.

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:34.487
Next week,

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.156
both leaders are scheduled to testify

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:37.123
before the Senate Armed

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:37.957
Services Committee.

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:40.026
In the House Armed Services Committee

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:41.494
on DOD's budget posture

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:44.330
and our Future Year's Defense Program.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:45.498
Again, the secretary

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:46.432
and the chairman look forward

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:47.367
to working with Congress

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:48.635
to provide our service members

00:02:48.635 --> 00:02:49.669
serving around the world

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:50.537
with the resources

00:02:50.537 --> 00:02:51.871
that they need to accomplish

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:53.473
DOD's mission

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:54.574
and strengthen America's

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:55.475
national security

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:58.578
for the 21st century and beyond.

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:00.213
Finally, on Wednesday, Secretary

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:00.980
Austin unveiled

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.382
a comprehensive plan aimed

00:03:02.382 --> 00:03:03.383
at improving the lives

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:05.051
of our dedicated military force

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:06.219
and their families.

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:07.320
The new plan consists

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.788
of six additional actions

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:09.756
that address essential

00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:11.424
needs in education,

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:12.358
child care,

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:14.761
parental leave and career advancement.

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:15.762
The Department of Defense

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:17.363
is committed to working with Congress

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:18.798
and other stakeholders

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:20.166
to ensure the successful

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:22.068
implementation of these measures.

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:23.002
The plan directs

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.971
the implementation of the following

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:26.573
universal pre-kindergarten

00:03:26.573 --> 00:03:28.708
DOD education activity, schools,

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:30.009
dependent care,

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:31.344
flexible spending accounts

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:32.912
for service members

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.647
promoting awareness of new military

00:03:34.647 --> 00:03:36.482
parental leave benefits

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.351
improvements to the exceptional family

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:39.886
member program,

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:41.154
expanded spouse

00:03:41.154 --> 00:03:43.056
eligibility for career advancement

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:45.258
account financial assistance,

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:47.493
and continuing efforts for portability

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:49.295
for professional licenses

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:51.297
for military families.

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:52.332
Secretary Austin

00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:53.433
and the Department of Defense

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:54.067
are dedicated

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:55.568
to enhancing the quality of life

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:56.536
for our servicemen

00:03:56.536 --> 00:03:57.637
and their families

00:03:57.637 --> 00:03:59.072
through these new measures.

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:00.273
The DOD will collaborate

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:01.641
with Congress and state partners

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:03.710
to ensure the successful implementation

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:06.179
and ongoing support of these initiatives.

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:08.481
The Memorandum and additional information

00:04:08.481 --> 00:04:10.750
can be found on the DOD website.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:11.851
Just have a couple of new details

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:12.285
that we got

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:13.620
from the Pentagon press secretary.

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:14.754
They're specifically

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:16.155
that the fighter jets

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:17.223
that carried out this air

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:19.025
strike on these Iran and Iran

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:21.361
backed facilities in Syria were two U.S.

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:23.196
Air Force F-15

00:04:23.196 --> 00:04:24.130
fighter aircraft,

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.999
and they actually struck two facilities

00:04:25.999 --> 00:04:27.667
and we were told earlier today

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:29.068
that those facilities were

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:30.870
where Iranian proxy groups

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.672
were housing some munitions

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:34.240
and also using as a base

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:35.708
to gather intelligence.

00:04:35.708 --> 00:04:37.810
Now, we're also told by by writer

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:38.077
there

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:40.179
that the Pentagon is still assessing

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:42.015
the number of militant casualties

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:42.915
that actually resulted

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:43.683
from that airstrike.

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:44.584
It is unclear

00:04:44.584 --> 00:04:46.319
how many people actually died there.

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:48.321
However, a UK based

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:49.822
human rights monitoring

00:04:49.822 --> 00:04:50.890
group says that there were at least

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.892
eight killed as a result of that U.S.

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:53.693
airstrike.

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:54.027
But look,

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:55.328
there were a lot of questions

00:04:55.328 --> 00:04:56.596
here about why

00:04:56.596 --> 00:04:58.264
that couldn't have been that that U.S.

00:04:58.264 --> 00:04:59.732
that Iranian drone strike

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:01.367
could not have been prevented. Right.

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:02.135
Because

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:03.569
the point was made

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:05.672
that these drones don't move very quickly

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:07.240
and that perhaps the base

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.441
could have taken some measures

00:05:08.441 --> 00:05:09.575
to try to take it down

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:12.512
before it crashed into that facility.

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:13.413
That was housing U.S.

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:14.147
personnel

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:15.615
and the question of the answer

00:05:15.615 --> 00:05:16.749
that we got from the Pentagon

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:17.350
press secretary

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:18.084
there was that they're

00:05:18.084 --> 00:05:20.219
essentially assessing what happened here.

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:21.721
It is his understanding

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:23.690
that the radar was all operating

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:24.524
pretty correctly

00:05:24.524 --> 00:05:26.225
and so the question now is

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:28.294
what can they do better to mitigate

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:30.129
that potential risk in the future?

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:31.331
And he did say that U.S.

00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:32.198
Central Command

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:34.233
is carrying out an assessment right now.

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:35.802
About how they can better protect U.S.

00:05:35.802 --> 00:05:37.136
troops and personnel stationed there.

00:05:38.371 --> 00:05:38.805
Only the

00:05:38.805 --> 00:05:39.339
latest in

00:05:39.339 --> 00:05:40.473
a round of attacks

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:42.575
from these Iranian backed groups.

00:05:42.575 --> 00:05:45.945
Some 80 drone or rocket attacks on U.S.

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:46.879
troops in that region

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:48.981
since the beginning of 2021.

00:05:48.981 --> 00:05:50.383
Natasha Bertrand from the Pentagon,

00:05:50.383 --> 00:05:51.084
thank you so much.

00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:52.318
Let's get some perspective now

00:05:52.318 --> 00:05:53.252
from retired Brigadier

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:54.587
General Peter Zack.

00:05:54.587 --> 00:05:55.488
He's a Wilson Center

00:05:55.488 --> 00:05:57.690
global fellow at the Kennan Institute.

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.759
Sir, thank you so much for being with us.

00:06:00.226 --> 00:06:01.761
And as we noted, that statistic.

00:06:01.761 --> 00:06:04.230
78 drone or rocket attacks on U.S.

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:06.466
troops in that area since 2021.

00:06:06.733 --> 00:06:07.700
Obviously

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:08.735
their Brigadier General, Pat

00:06:08.735 --> 00:06:10.303
Ryder, asked about the security

00:06:10.303 --> 00:06:11.771
of these facilities.

00:06:11.771 --> 00:06:14.173
What the focus of the United States

00:06:14.173 --> 00:06:15.375
from a security perspective

00:06:15.375 --> 00:06:16.776
obviously is on Eastern Europe.

00:06:16.776 --> 00:06:18.044
It's on the Pacific.

00:06:18.044 --> 00:06:20.113
What is enough being done to protect

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:23.282
and fortify our assets in Syria?

00:06:23.282 --> 00:06:24.150
In this fight

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:25.952
continuing fight against ISIS

00:06:28.521 --> 00:06:29.622
I believe

00:06:29.622 --> 00:06:31.758
that the forces on the ground

00:06:31.758 --> 00:06:33.393
force protection

00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:35.762
in these type of environments

00:06:36.596 --> 00:06:37.263
now I've seen

00:06:37.263 --> 00:06:40.600
it is paramount paramount and

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:43.436
and but the nature of war

00:06:43.436 --> 00:06:46.372
the unpredictability of conflict

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:48.674
It's not perfect.

00:06:48.674 --> 00:06:50.143
It's not a perfect science.

00:06:50.143 --> 00:06:52.078
And sometimes

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:55.982
missiles or drones will get through.

00:06:57.216 --> 00:06:59.752
I think that what we would know

00:06:59.786 --> 00:07:02.054
is, is that this is an in

00:07:02.054 --> 00:07:04.090
and when you look at the whole picture,

00:07:04.791 --> 00:07:06.159
fairly rare.

00:07:06.159 --> 00:07:08.761
But but it did happen.

00:07:09.295 --> 00:07:11.197
78 attacks apparently

00:07:11.197 --> 00:07:12.698
over the last few years

00:07:12.698 --> 00:07:15.001
between Syria and Iraq.

00:07:15.001 --> 00:07:16.235
And yes.

00:07:16.235 --> 00:07:18.037
But I got to believe those

00:07:18.037 --> 00:07:20.206
those ground commanders

00:07:20.206 --> 00:07:23.176
whose responsibility is pay varied.

00:07:23.309 --> 00:07:25.845
No one is force protection

00:07:26.646 --> 00:07:29.248
for offensive operations.

00:07:29.248 --> 00:07:32.018
And General, we know that Iran often uses

00:07:32.018 --> 00:07:33.186
these proxy groups

00:07:33.186 --> 00:07:34.654
to carry out these attacks,

00:07:34.654 --> 00:07:35.488
which is what

00:07:35.488 --> 00:07:37.590
apparently reportedly happened here.

00:07:37.924 --> 00:07:40.059
Help us understand why they do that.

00:07:40.092 --> 00:07:40.993
Does that allow them

00:07:40.993 --> 00:07:42.662
to keep their hands clean, as it were?

00:07:42.662 --> 00:07:43.563
We heard that reporter

00:07:43.563 --> 00:07:44.931
trying to press

00:07:44.931 --> 00:07:45.998
the general there about

00:07:45.998 --> 00:07:47.667
if Iran was responsible

00:07:47.667 --> 00:07:48.734
for this American death.

00:07:48.734 --> 00:07:50.236
And he didn't quite

00:07:50.236 --> 00:07:52.538
stop short of saying that they were

00:07:52.538 --> 00:07:53.606
What do you make of all of that?

00:07:55.308 --> 00:07:56.943
Well, the proxy forces, when

00:07:56.943 --> 00:07:58.010
we hear of that,

00:07:58.010 --> 00:07:59.011
we think of

00:07:59.011 --> 00:07:59.679
first of all,

00:07:59.679 --> 00:08:02.248
there is the IRGC revolution guard.

00:08:02.415 --> 00:08:04.851
And they kind of are the, if you will,

00:08:05.751 --> 00:08:08.421
managing and quarterbacking ever.

00:08:08.688 --> 00:08:11.290
You've got Shia militias in there

00:08:12.091 --> 00:08:14.494
you've got locals.

00:08:16.095 --> 00:08:18.731
And you have also,

00:08:19.365 --> 00:08:22.602
in fact, Dara, czar where we saw the

00:08:23.936 --> 00:08:26.806
attack yesterday was where

00:08:26.806 --> 00:08:31.444
sight of a very, very, very tough U.S.

00:08:32.278 --> 00:08:34.347
and ally engagement

00:08:34.747 --> 00:08:37.149
